          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:143b42d1c65adff7d3381c97605867d546ee1302f8442950ff4376bb0b259b4c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://training/pretrain.py#L241-L258",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a8a8ad81c07c14bc264acf2935ef8836b8362450b01847fedbe1930b02caeb16:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_eb97c879727042448a145dfc771edaf4",
      "statement": "`GPTOSS.forward` embeds `(B, T)` token IDs, iterates through the ordered blocks while collecting each block's auxiliary loss, applies final RMSNorm and the LM head, and returns logits of shape `(B, T, vocab_size)` plus the mean auxiliary-loss scalar.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/transformer.py#L138-L153",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2ce8317e8fc28f7bc1cecd29be681d176bdb47c3bdff6e6c6721cb98a5bc1614:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/transformer.py#L156-L170",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6cd294d74e6ea013abd7fa527745c059d756389b6b3bc7e7a0450a3c356ccf72:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/transformer.py#L186-L227",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:52783c07db9d7eb20febbe324704ed062617efbb773964f712954562f0292a20:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_696cb0cd33fb42a8abbf837b2662f69d",
      "statement": "Each `GPTOSSBlock` implements two ordered pre-norm residual sublayers: attention receives `norm1(x)`, then MoE receives `norm2` of the attention-updated stream; both residual additions preserve the model hidden width.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/transformer.py#L138-L153",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2ce8317e8fc28f7bc1cecd29be681d176bdb47c3bdff6e6c6721cb98a5bc1614:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bd291f5cf51146458724769103b55140",
      "statement": "Attention uses GQA with `n_heads` query heads and `n_kv_heads` key/value heads, applies YaRN RoPE to Q and K, repeats K/V by `n_heads // n_kv_heads`, and selects sliding-window attention on even layer indices versus full causal attention on odd indices.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/attention.py#L134-L177",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:93ade5f758d4ff7350c04139708ee63ac24abba75e4e07f4242f937444bd40aa:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/attention.py#L179-L215",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8637fb7ff2f1cf553a4cde99cda59083c242f7df3f9930b2fc98d5bf29a5e42a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/attention.py#L78-L122",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c5b9264dfe400d0683ad704e2630eaea137ea6b4a95c2ae8f9fa5653286875d4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_18a554089b5644b3b601303bf66c599a",
      "statement": "When enabled, global-layer RoPE pruning freezes `head_dim // 4` leading RoPE dimensions, while the odd-layer/full-attention convention means an odd total layer count can leave the final layer windowed and therefore unpruned; `ModelConfig` emits a warning for that case.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/attention.py#L151-L176",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:30bf0b753e004ca89a1dbd832ef2a958b0e8abf2d615b8064b2f15456e756bab:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/transformer.py#L101-L107",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0440b874d5aaa6c0092876ae6b68cc9d5188c055dd86b465c0d1e415eb3ec648:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/yarn.py#L48-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4fc9b9d294af45a54129e87462cf2fff05db579ee55e3f314b689230e5b351a9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_654c588624ff4d70a3e6ca04376fef6e",
      "statement": "MoE routing flattens `(B,T,D)` tokens, computes FP32 gate probabilities, selects and renormalizes top-k routed experts, dispatches their weighted SwiGLU outputs, adds all configured shared experts, restores `(B,T,D)`, and returns a per-layer load-balancing loss that `GPTOSS` averages across layers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/moe.py#L24-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:418fdcdd18bed1e21d78aa4b9cb60472381235768898643074125eb9a27b1e2f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/moe.py#L64-L105",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:744227fb09aa7ff7cec77482e78e920d84cbdce060ca05e670c4e4349d2bac3b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/transformer.py#L201-L227",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b9c452b17746f626201ab153e3d3122aae900e1bbba770e33bbd7858cb62a9c6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_848e782ec6ee49e68067a31823abef82",
      "statement": "`ModelConfig` fails fast on the shape and routing invariants required by runtime tensor operations: positive dimensions, `n_heads % n_kv_heads == 0`, `n_heads * head_dim == d_model`, even `head_dim`, and `0 < n_activated_experts <= n_routed_experts` with nonnegative shared-expert count.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/transformer.py#L51-L88",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d4949603d360590e94dc6eaa189fb312c84762cc57c9affbf7db2bc61f2323a1:"
